    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d681">

                <pb facs="0695" n="689" sameAs="frus:frus1942v02/pg689"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00115 Pacific War/179: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Consul at Nouméa (MacVitty)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-02-19T18:00:00-04:00">February 19,
                            1942—6 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>29. Your 22, February 17, 5 p.m. You may inform the High Commissioner that in all
                    matters relating to the defense of New Caledonia this Government is prepared to
                    recognize that the French National Committee has authority over the Island and
                    deals with the representatives of General de Gaulle in all matters relating to
                    its defense.</p>
                <p>You may also inform the High Commissioner that this Government has warned the
                    Government of Vichy against taking any action in these colonies which might give
                    the appearance of acting under Japanese duress.<anchor n="71" xml:id="d681-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
